  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "Everything that comes straight from a household's keys: docs/API.md (Identity model, Keys). A household has one 32-byte secret per key epoch; each key below is HKDF of one epoch's secret.",
    "Bytes are base64url without padding unless a field says hex or base64; strings are UTF-8; \"|\" joins the parts of a message, with nothing around it.",
    "HKDF is HKDF-SHA256 with salt \"petcam\" and 32 bytes out; HMAC is HMAC-SHA256; AES-GCM is AES-256-GCM with a 12-byte nonce and a 16-byte tag.",
    "Made by server/scripts/vectors.mjs from fixed keys that were made up for these files; nothing here was ever a real home's. No vector is ever removed: a format the apps stop opening stays, as one that must fail. Read by SharedTests/KeyVectorTests.swift and server/test/vectors.test.ts."
  ],
  "household_id": "11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555",
  "how": {
    "key": "HKDF-SHA256(the epoch's secret, salt \"petcam\", info the key's name, 32 bytes)",
    "join_token": "base64url of the petcam.join.v1 key: the only derivative the server ever sees, and only the current epoch's",
    "join_token_hash": "base64url(SHA-256(UTF-8 of the join token's text)): what the server keeps",
    "from_before": "petcam.media.v1 (unbound media, until 2026-11-03) and petcam.invite.nonce.v1 (a member nonce that left the key out, until 2026-11-10) are keys the apps no longer use: sealed-v1.json and invite-v1.json have what they made, as failures"
  },
